Lab: Version Control for OpenShift Pipelines
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Store Tekton pipeline YAML files in a Git repository using an organized directory structure
Apply semantic versioning to pipeline definitions using labels, Git tags, and a version manager script
Track pipeline changes across environments using Git branches and commit history
Implement a rollback procedure to restore a previous pipeline version using Git tags
Validate pipeline YAML files before committing changes to version control
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Git version control concepts (init, add, commit, tag, branch)
Familiarity with YAML file structure and syntax
Knowledge of CI/CD pipeline fundamentals (Tekton Pipelines and Tasks)
Experience with command-line interface operations on Linux
Basic knowledge of OpenShift or Kubernetes environments
This lab runs entirely on the local filesystem using Git. No live OpenShift cluster is required to complete the tasks, since all oc apply commands are shown for reference only. All work should be performed in an isolated, self-owned practice environment.

